Back in 2024   I was asked to give a talk for the back then online only OpenSource Observabillity Day,   while I`m not a big fan of online only events, there really was a gap
that needed to be filled.   Sure we got OSMC,  there used to be Monitorama which happened iirc 2x in Europe,  and there is the (close to impossible to attend) o11yday before Kubecon.
But there is no event where the Open Source obvservabillty  community meets.    Last year while chatting with Peter Zaitzev  I already hinted  at maybe doing an in peson OSoday in 
Gent as a Fringe event to CfgMgmtCamp.   It would be an ideal fit as a number of people with this interrest would already be around for Fosdem or CfgMgmtCamp so it would be
only one trip for multiple events . 

So now I`m really happen to announce that we are making this happen. 

Open Source Observability day 2027 will happen in person in Ghent.   
You can expect a variety of O11y topics,   Different tools wil be present to tell you what they have been working on , but we'll 
also look at the consumers of the tools and how they improved their ecosystem by using some of these tools.

So if you have an interresting tool / story, don't hesitate to submit a proposal to our CFP.

Obviously just visiting is also an option ..  Our registration is open , the event is free but we'd love to know how many of you we can expect. 

And if there is an talk that doesn't match your interrest at a certain timeslot, there are still more community events happening 
in the same building that day , check out the CfgMgmtCamp Fringe :) 





